CAT = "sgsecPatrol"; SEG = "PAT"
# Patrols, defects, casualties and incident reporting: PLRD refresher training package (summary of
# SEC-ICM-1003-1.1 Incident Response and SEC-SOP-1007-1.1 Guard and Patrol), Conduct Regulations
# 2009 reg 5, SCDF Civil Defence Emergency Handbook (10th ed., 2026).
Q = [
("What are the two core duties of a security officer?",
 "Protecting lives and property", ["Collecting rent and service fees", "Cleaning and building upkeep", "Leasing units and marketing"],
 "The PLRD package sums up an officer's duties as protecting lives and property and keeping the guarded premises safe and secure."),
("Why should an officer learn the layout of the building they guard?",
 "To respond faster", ["To redraw floor plans", "To value the property", "To shorten the reports"],
 "Knowing the layout makes patrolling easier, speeds up the response to an emergency and lets the officer direct visitors."),
("On patrol, an officer notices faulty emergency exit signage. What should they do?",
 "Report the defect", ["Rewire the sign themselves", "Take the sign down", "Wait for a complaint"],
 "Faulty emergency signage is on the PLRD list of defects to report to the Control Room, with faulty lighting, burst pipes, leaking sprinklers, gas leaks, faulty doors and windows and broken car park barriers."),
("Which patrol finding is on PLRD's list of defects to report to the Control Room?",
 "A leaking sprinkler", ["A tenant's late rent", "A shop's new signage", "A full recycling bin"],
 "Leaking sprinkler systems are among the defects officers report. Rent and shop signage are management matters, not safety defects."),
("Which safety gear should an officer wear to patrol a construction site?",
 "Helmet, gloves and boots", ["Cap, vest and sunglasses", "Mask, apron and earmuffs", "Raincoat, scarf and sandals"],
 "The PLRD package lists a safety helmet, safety gloves and safety boots for patrols on construction sites."),
("A hose reel is leaking and the floor is very wet. After informing the Control Room, what should the officer ask for?",
 "Repairs, tape and a sign", ["A mop from the tenants", "A plumber's written quote", "Leave to shut the building"],
 "The scenario asks the Control Room to get the maintenance team to repair the reel and for cordon tape and a \"Danger Keep Out\" sign to be brought."),
("At what height should cordon tape be set around a wet floor hazard?",
 "Waist level", ["Ankle level", "Head level", "Knee level"],
 "The PLRD scenario says to cordon the area at waist level so it is easy to see and hard to walk through."),
("Which way should a \"Danger Keep Out\" sign face when placed at a cordon?",
 "Outwards", ["Inwards", "Upwards", "Sideways"],
 "The sign faces outwards so people approaching can read it clearly and stay away from the area."),
("Once a cordoned leak has been repaired, what should the officer do before removing the tape?",
 "Confirm the area is safe", ["Let the cleaner decide", "Wait for the next shift", "Ask a tenant to walk it"],
 "The officer checks the area is safe before removing the cordon tape and sign, then informs the Control Room and records the incident."),
("A person collapses in the lobby. After reporting to the Control Room, who should be told to call SCDF?",
 "Management", ["The casualty's family", "A passing shopper", "The building's cleaner"],
 "In the PLRD scenario, the officer reports to the Control Room and informs management to call SCDF, then stays with the casualty and reassures them."),
("Which details of a conscious casualty should the officer note for the report?",
 "Name, NRIC and contact details", ["Blood group and allergies only", "Employer and monthly salary", "Car plate and insurer's name"],
 "The officer notes the casualty's name, NRIC number, contact details and address for reporting while waiting with them."),
("After paramedics take a casualty away, what should the officer update the Control Room with?",
 "The receiving hospital", ["The casualty's diagnosis", "The ambulance's plate", "The bill for the ride"],
 "The officer updates the Control Room on the paramedic who took over the case and which hospital the casualty was taken to, then records the incident."),
("On patrol, an officer sees a big fire on the third floor. What is the first action?",
 "Break the nearest call point", ["Search every unit for people", "Film the fire as evidence", "Wait for the alarm to ring"],
 "The PLRD scenario starts with running to the nearest call point and breaking the glass to activate the fire alarm, then informing the Control Room and management."),
("Several office workers have trouble breathing and two collapse. There is a strange chemical smell. What should the officer do first?",
 "Cover nose and mouth, evacuate", ["Give first aid to each person", "Turn the air-conditioning up", "Wait inside the unit for help"],
 "The PLRD scenario says to cover nose and mouth with a cloth and evacuate the people, then inform the Control Room, the Police and SCDF, and cordon off the area."),
("After a suspected chemical incident, which two records should the officer complete at the guardhouse?",
 "Occurrence Book and Incident Report", ["Key Movement Book and visitor log", "Lost and Found Book and roster", "Attendance sheet and leave form"],
 "Once back at the guardhouse, the officer updates the Occurrence Book and raises an Incident Report."),
("Which is a sign that someone may be carrying out unauthorised surveillance of the premises?",
 "Filming the entrances", ["Buying lunch nearby", "Asking for the toilets", "Waiting for a lift"],
 "PLRD lists recording the premises with cameras, loitering near restricted areas, posing as maintenance staff and befriending officers for shift details as signs of unauthorised surveillance."),
("A friendly \"vendor\" keeps chatting to officers about shift change times. This is a sign of:",
 "Hostile surveillance", ["Good customer relations", "A job interview request", "A routine safety audit"],
 "Befriending security or maintenance teams to learn shift patterns and security measures is a listed sign of someone conducting surveillance."),
("An officer becomes aware that someone is conducting surveillance of the guarded premises. Under regulation 5, the officer must:",
 "Lodge a police report", ["Confront the person directly", "Raise it at the monthly meeting", "Post a warning online"],
 "Regulation 5(1) requires a licensed officer who patrols or guards premises to lodge a police report without undue delay when aware of surveillance by anyone other than a law enforcement officer."),
("Which behaviour is on PLRD's list of suspicious behaviour?",
 "Leaving a parcel and walking off", ["Holding a door open for others", "Reading the building directory", "Queuing at the lift lobby"],
 "PLRD lists placing an object or parcel within or outside the premises before leaving the area, along with no valid pass, sweating profusely, avoiding eye contact and avoiding CCTV."),
("A man keeps turning his face away from every CCTV camera on his route. PLRD treats this as:",
 "Suspicious behaviour", ["Normal camera shyness", "Proof of a crime", "A medical symptom"],
 "Avoiding being captured on CCTV is a listed type of suspicious behaviour. It is a reason to watch and report, not proof of an offence."),
("Which clothing may mark a person as suspicious under PLRD guidance?",
 "Baggy, oversized clothes", ["A school uniform", "A company polo shirt", "A raincoat in the rain"],
 "Baggy, oversized clothing that could conceal objects, face-covering caps or helmets, and wires dangling from clothes are listed as inappropriate attire that may mark a suspicious person."),
("An officer sees a man filming the building and acting suspiciously. What should be noted first?",
 "His description", ["His camera model", "His car's colour", "His lunch order"],
 "The PLRD scenario starts with noting a detailed description: age, sex, race, height and features such as a beard or moustache."),
("In that filming case, what should the Control Room be asked to do?",
 "Watch him on CCTV", ["Switch off the cameras", "Lock all exits at once", "Announce him on the PA"],
 "The Control Room is asked to tilt a camera to monitor the man and to call the police, before the supervisor or management is told."),
("When police arrive at an incident the officer reported, what should the officer hand over?",
 "The evidence collected", ["The suspect's wallet", "The tenancy list", "The duty roster"],
 "The officer briefs the police officer on the incident and hands over evidence such as photographs taken discreetly on the phone."),
("Before an incident is closed, which details of the attending police officer should be recorded?",
 "Name, ID and division", ["Home address and age", "Rank and car colour", "Phone and birthday"],
 "The PLRD package says to get the police officer's name, ID and division and update the Control Room that the case has been handed over."),
("A car drives slowly past the main gate three times. What should the officer record?",
 "Plate, make, model, colour", ["The driver's job and age", "The radio station playing", "The car's road tax expiry"],
 "The officer records the registration number, make, model and colour, watches the driver's behaviour, looks for other passengers and for vehicle-borne IED signs, then informs the Control Room."),
("How is an incident recorded once the matter is handed over?",
 "As the employer's procedures set", ["In whatever way the officer likes", "Only if the client asks for it", "In a personal phone note"],
 "Every PLRD scenario ends with updating the Control Room and recording the incident according to the employer's procedures."),
("Which number should an officer call to report a gas pipe leakage from piped town gas?",
 "1800 752 1800", ["1800 778 8888", "1800 342 5222", "1800 241 7711"],
 "SCDF's handbook gives 1800 752 1800 (City Energy) for piped town gas leaks, called from a safe distance. The others are SP PowerGrid, the Building and Construction Authority and HDB's EMSU."),
]
